    "_class_weight_multiplier_note": "unweighted, the 5 signal sub-classes' train-split sumw was Wcb 0.38% / t2_bc 0.16% / t2_bb 0.21% / t3_bbc 0.09% / t2_bc_proxy 99.16% (proxy pulled unthinned from the whole 16-sample background pool, Cabibbo-favoured W->cs vastly outnumbers the dedicated Vcb sample) -- the BDT loss was ~99% 'find a proxy-like jet' and Wcb was noise in the gradient. These multipliers retarget train-split positive-class sumw shares to Wcb 58% / t2_bc 8% / t2_bb 14% / t3_bbc 12% / proxy 8% (was 56/12/12/8/12, before that 50/12/12/6/20; Wcb prioritised: ~2/3 of SR significance; proxy now capped at 12%, i.e. on par with true t2_bc rather than 632x it). Applied at LOAD time (train.py/scan_keep_prob.py) to TRAIN and VALID weight only -- TEST is left at raw physics weight so reported AUC/working-points/per-class efficiency stay physically meaningful. Computed from presel_v3_kp50 train raw sumw (Wcb 85.78, t2_bc 35.45, t2_bb 48.47, t3_bbc 19.50, proxy 22406.01); independent of background_keep_prob (only touches topology==0). Revisit the 12/12/6 split and the 20% proxy cap once a real per-class SR-significance number exists.",
